[34.653511, "o", "736:RULES APPLYING TO AUTHORISED OFFICERS\r\n737:(1) An authorised officer shall carry a document of identity written in English, French and\r\n738:the language of the authorised officer (if different) in a form agreed by the Contracting Parties on\r\n740:(2) Any orders to stop given by an authorised officer shall be given by the appropriate signal\r\n742:(3) On boarding a vessel an authorised officer shall exhibit his document of identity.\r\n744:(4) On boarding a vessel an authorised officer may require the master of the vessel to exhibit\r\n754:shall immediately be endorsed upon it by the authorised officer or on some other official document\r\n756:(5) On each occasion on which an authorised officer boards a vessel, he shall draw up a\r\n759:(6) This report shall be drawn up in the language of the authorised officer and shown to the\r\n761:any remarks he or any member of his crew may wish to make. The authorised officer shall sign\r\n766:(7) Whenever an authorised officer observes a vessel infringing the provisions of the Con\r\n771:(8) Ships carrying authorised officers, which may be vessels as defined in article 1 (2), shall\r\n773:Parties on the request of the depositary Government. Authorised officers shall exercise their powers\r\n778:Authorised Officer (to be filled in in block letters)\r\n837:24. Comments by Authorised Officer.\r\n842:Signature of Authorised Officer ...................\r\n843:The above report was prepared and signed by the Authorised Officer in our presence.\r\n"]
